159
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
and a great relief

160
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
in a lot of cases,

161
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
especially if they are 18,

162
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
11 months, two weeks

163
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
and seven days

164
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
or three days or whatever you know.

165
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Here's what I do.

166
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
First of all,

167
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
my Eagle scoutmaster conferences

168
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
are not very formal

169
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
and they're pretty brief,

170
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
And here's the reason why

171
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Most of the time I've been

172
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,000
in a pretty continuous dialogue

173
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
with a scout who is getting ready

174
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
to go to an Eagle border review.

175
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
He's been working on a project.

176
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
He's been

177
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
has had at minimum

178
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
10 months of a leadership position in the Troop,

179
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,000
So we've had

180
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
plenty of opportunity

181
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
to talk back and forth,

182
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
And so the first thing I will do

183
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
is I will reassure him

184
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
that he's a quality guy

185
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
that he did all the work that he needed to do

186
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
and that he should be very pleased

187
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
with what he has done.

188
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
I'll give him an encapsulated evaluation,

189
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
My encapsulated evaluation

190
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
of him as a leader,

191
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
which will typically be: you know,

192
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
you're a very capable leader,

193
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
You're very well.

194
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
I remember several instances where

195
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
it got difficult for you,

196
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
but you rose to the challenge

197
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
and you should be very satisfied.

198
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
So putting him at ease

199
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
is a pretty important thing.

200
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
And then, talking a little bit

201
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,000
about the border review,

202
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,000
it's much like all the other

203
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
boards of review that you've had.

204
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
There'll be some more people there.

205
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
They'll be asking more questions

206
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
than usual

207
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
And they will be evaluating

208
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
your Eagle project- and you know

209
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
it's quite a big deal-

210
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
recommending whether or not

211
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
you should become an Eagle Scout.

212
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
I have no doubt in my mind

213
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
that they will recommend you

214
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
become an Eagle Scout.

215
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
But let's prepare a little bit

216
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,000
for the types of questions

217
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,000
you're going to be asked.

218
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Now, what kinds of questions

219
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
do you imagine they're going to ask you?

220
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
And if I met with you know,

221
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
kind of a blank stare.

222
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
we'll start teasing that out a little bit

223
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,000
by this method of socratic questioning,

224
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
if you want to put a fancy name to it,

225
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
which is basically just, you know,

226
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
asking questions to help people

227
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
hone their thinking

228
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
and to help them be on their feet

229
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
in a conversation.

230
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
It also helps them be unexpected

231
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:48,000
and be able to be flexible

232
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
in commanding the subject

233
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
that they're working with

234
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
and being able to answer questions

235
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,000
directed to them.

236
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
So I will get kind of pushy

237
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,000
with my questions

238
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
And my scouts by this time

239
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
have learned to understand

240
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
that this is a little game that we play,

241
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
that I'm not trying to be mean

242
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,000
or judgmental

243
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
or I'm not disappointed in them

244
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
in some way,

245
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
But I ask these hard questions

246
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
because it helps them think.

247
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
it helps them think forward

248
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
and helps them prepare

249
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,000
and also should help them discover

250
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
any places where they are unprepared

251
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
or where they're a little weak

252
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
in their thinking or knowledge.

253
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
So it's a bit of a game.

254
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,000
So tell me how your project

255
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
qualifies to be considered

256
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
a fulfillment of the requirement

257
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
for Eagle

258
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
And once in a while

259
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
I'll get a blank stare back.

260
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
I'll say, well, tell me what the

261
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
requirement for Eagle is.

262
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,000
so far as the project is concerned,

263
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
I'll say, well,

264
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,000
open the Scout Handbook there,

265
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,000
read it.

266
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Okay, now defend your project

267
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
based on that requirement.

268
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Tell me what you did as a leader.

269
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Tell me why you think that

270
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
that experience should fulfill

271
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
the requirement for Eagle.

272
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
so far as leadership is concerned,

273
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
What were your most difficult decisions?

274
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
What was the most difficult time

275
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
you had as a leader?

276
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
What do you figure you got really good?

277
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
How do you figure you contributed to your troop?

278
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
What were your best achievements

279
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
as a leader in your opinion?

280
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Now, why was that a great achievement

281
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Or why was that a difficult time?

282
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:29,000
And, like I said, I'm kind of pushy

283
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:33,000
And then I can also let them

284
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
turn the tables on me

285
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
and ask me difficult questions

286
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,000
and kind of push me around it.

287
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Like I say, if you work it right,

288
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
it's kind of a game that you play

289
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,000
with your Scouts

290
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
And you want them to push back,

291
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
You want them to defend themselves

292
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,000
and their ideas,

293
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
And that's, you know,

294
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
the method of Socratic Questioning.

295
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
That's what really makes it work.

296
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
So Will. I hope that helps you a little bit.

297
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Once again, congratulations,

298
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
And I would love to hear from any of you

299
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
who have other input into

300
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,000
what should be discussed

301
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
or how to conduct a Scout Masters conference

302
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
with an Eagle candidate.

303
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
So do get in touch.

